"The family's renderer places (legit.json's renderer, read as ranks by tools/xdiff_bn4.py bn4_renderer) are ranked without a hit's spark its attack struck with (the fourth kind's 0x04, tools/xdiff_bn4.py ranks_into, which takes it out of the drawn it ranks; thunderman_v1's cloud at t787 and windman_v1's companions at t183 the same, behind a spark one game alone still draws): the spark is each engine's own effect, its sprite state and its life its own art's (allowed, \"the hit's spark, each engine's own\"), and the renderer hands it a place from the same running count as every object it draws (BN4's and BN6's renderer, the same code), so while one game's spark is drawn and the other's has ended it takes a rank in one game alone and moves the ranks of the family's objects drawn after it. In fireman_v1 the spark of his flame's hit on MegaMan (struck at t256) runs its own art's animation (BN4's counts 2,1,0,1,0,... BN6's 1,0,1,0,...) and ends at BN6's t272 while BN4's is drawn on (place 0x40 at t271, between his flames, 0x2F, and his companion, 0x2D): his companion's rank 3 in BN4 and 2 in BN6 at t271 with it ranked, 2 in both without. Its own places, never ranked, read as no place in both games, as an object never drawn"
